  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Support card synergy determines training efficiency—run 6 support cards that share at least 3 bonuses (Training Effect Up, Hint Rate Up, or Event Rate Up) to maximise the combined stat gains per training session.",
      "Factor inheritance from parent Uma Musume stacks—prioritise parents with 3-star Speed factors for Sprint distance races; 3-star Stamina for Long distance. Blue Star factors provide stat bonus at training completion and are worth more than identical green factors.",
      "URA Finals (first scenario) is the recommended mastery scenario—complete it 10+ times before attempting Aoharu Cup or Mecha Musume scenarios to understand base stat ceilings and event choice optimisation.",
      "Training order within a week matters: prioritise the training action with the highest SSR support card's bonus (displayed as yellow shimmer) over raw stat need, as support card bonus events are the highest per-turn value actions.",
      "Race participation (non-mandatory) improves race aptitude—race in your Uma Musume's weakest distance aptitude 3 times per scenario to raise it from C to B rank, which increases performance by 8% in that distance category."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "サポートカードのシナジーがトレーニング効率を決定する。トレーニング効果アップ、ヒント発生率アップ、イベント発生率アップの少なくとも3つのボーナスを共有する6枚のサポートカードでデッキを組み、セッションごとの統合ステータス増加を最大化する。",
      "親ウマ娘からの因子継承は積み重なる。スプリント距離レースには3つ星スピード因子を持つ親を優先。長距離には3つ星スタミナ。青色星の因子はトレーニング完了時にステータスボーナスを提供し、同一の緑色因子より価値が高い。",
      "URAファイナルズ（最初のシナリオ）は推奨の習熟シナリオ。基本ステータスの上限とイベント選択の最適化を理解するために、青春杯またはメカウマ娘シナリオを試みる前に10回以上完走する。",
      "1週間のトレーニング順序が重要。SSRサポートカードのボーナス（黄色いシマーとして表示）が最も高いトレーニングアクションを、生のステータスの必要性より優先する。サポートカードのボーナスイベントはターンあたり最高価値のアクション。",
      "レース参加（非必須）は適性を向上させる。各シナリオでウマ娘の最弱距離適性で3回レースに参加し、CからBランクに引き上げる。これはその距離カテゴリのパフォーマンスを8%向上させる。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Support Card Team Composition",
        "body": "A balanced support team for new players: 2 Speed support cards (primary stat), 2 Stamina (endurance for longer races), 1 Power (acceleration), 1 Friend card (the versatile wildcard slot). The Friend card slot should always use your highest-rarity Friend card regardless of bond level, as Friend events provide the most varied stat bonuses. Avoid running 3+ support cards of the same stat category until you have SSR cards in all slots—over-specialised teams cap one stat while leaving others critically low."
      },
      {
        "title": "Early Training Priority",
        "body": "In the first 6 months of a scenario (in-game), maintain all training stats within 15 points of each other. Diverging stat values by 30+ creates visible performance gaps in races against appropriately-built opponents. Use the Motivation Gauge (yellow bar above the Uma Musume) as your daily training guide—high motivation increases all training stat gains by 10%; low motivation should trigger rest or skill hint events rather than forced training."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Skill Selection Strategy",
        "body": "Skills in Uma Musume activate based on race position and distance—choose skills that match your race strategy (front-runner, pace-setter, closer, or late-surge). For front-runner builds: prioritise skills with \"First Spurt\" and \"Opening Lead\" in their name. For closer builds: \"Last Spurt\" and \"Final Corner\" skills trigger during the comeback phase. Mixed skills (position-independent) are the safest choice when strategy varies, but provide lower peak benefit than specialised options."
      },
      {
        "title": "Champions Meeting Preparation",
        "body": "Champions Meetings are limited-time multiplayer events with unique prize Uma Musume—participating requires completing a qualifying race with a trained Uma Musume at the minimum stat threshold. The qualifying threshold increases each season. Prioritise getting one Uma Musume to the current qualifying level over training multiple Uma Musume at lower stat levels; a single qualified entry with a high-scoring race provides more reward currency than 3 unqualified attempts."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Liga/Circuit End-Game Optimisation",
        "body": "The end-game circuit requires an Uma Musume with balanced stats above 2,500 in primary categories. The final optimisation loop: identify the highest stat the Uma Musume is closest to the next breakpoint in (stat breakpoints occur every 100 points and provide multiplier bonuses in races), focus final training sessions on that stat, then use Genius and special event choices to push above the next breakpoint. A well-timed breakpoint crossing in the final training week provides 5–8% stat multiplier improvement for all subsequent races."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Treating all training weeks equally—weeks with support card bonus events (yellow shimmer) provide 2–3× the stat gain of normal weeks; plan mandatory rest before high-bonus training weeks, not after them.",
      "Ignoring bond level building with support cards—higher bond levels with support cards trigger more unique events and higher stat bonuses; reach bond level 80 with your primary support card before the final scenario arc.",
      "Choosing skills based on name aesthetics rather than race strategy match—skill activation conditions are displayed in the skill description; selecting skills without reading conditions means equipping abilities that rarely activate.",
      "Not participating in free races during training—non-mandatory races improve aptitude and provide in-scenario tokens for exchanging rare training events; skipping them wastes both aptitude points and token income.",
      "Using Gacha currency on limited banners without checking the featured Uma Musume's competitive tier—limited banner Uma Musume vary significantly in strength; check tier lists before spending Jewel currency on banners."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "全てのトレーニング週を同等に扱う。サポートカードのボーナスイベント（黄色いシマー）のある週は通常の週より2〜3倍のステータス増加を提供する。高ボーナストレーニング週の後ではなく前に必須の休憩を計画する。",
      "サポートカードとのきずな構築を無視する。サポートカードとの高い絆レベルはよりユニークなイベントとより高いステータスボーナスをトリガーする。最終シナリオアーク前に主要サポートカードで絆レベル80に達する。",
      "名前の見た目に基づいてスキルを選ぶ。スキルの発動条件はスキルの説明に表示されている。条件を読まずにスキルを選ぶと、めったに発動しない能力を装備することになる。",
      "トレーニング中に自由レースに参加しない。非必須レースは適性を向上させ、レアトレーニングイベントの交換のためのシナリオ内トークンを提供する。スキップすると適性ポイントとトークン収入の両方が無駄になる。",
      "注目ウマ娘の競技ティアを確認せずにガチャ通貨を限定バナーに使う。限定バナーのウマ娘は強さが大きく異なる。ジュエル通貨をバナーに使う前にティアリストを確認する。"
    ]
